            "body": "Thanks for tracking this down, I hit the same failure on macOS (attn-gym installs, cutlass/triton have no wheels, so `torchtitan.models.common` can't import and no CPU unit test collects). Since #5231 the facade in `torchtitan/models/common/attn_gym.py` owns the \"attn_gym missing\" case, and the `linear_attention.py` import goes through it too, so I put the same deferral there for every export in #<new PR number>, keeping the error name/message the facade tests expect. ",
