  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "<!-- ciflow-pending -->\nThe following ciflow label(s) have been added but CI has not been triggered yet because the workflows are awaiting approval:\n\n- `ciflow/rl`\n- `ciflow/fake-pg`\n\nOnce a maintainer approves the workflows (scroll to the bottom of the PR page), the corresponding CI jobs will be triggered automatically. Please ping one of the reviewers if you do not have access to approve and run workflows.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-08T21:29:46Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5181#issuecomment-6069418191",
      "id": 6069418191,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-08T21:29:46Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "pytorch-bot[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks for tracking this down, I hit the same failure on macOS (attn-gym installs, cutlass/triton have no wheels, so `torchtitan.models.common` can't import and no CPU unit test collects). Since #5231 the facade in `torchtitan/models/common/attn_gym.py` owns the \"attn_gym missing\" case, and the `linear_attention.py` import goes through it too, so I put the same deferral there for every export in #<new PR number>, keeping the error name/message the facade tests expect. ",
      "created_at": "2026-10-17T06:25:24Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5181#issuecomment-6230661356",
      "id": 6230661356,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-17T06:25:24Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mkhilari"
      }
    },
